\end{longtable}

Note that $(\Id,-\Id)$ has no effect on $\mathbb{H}^2$. Therefore we can view $\mathbb{D}_T/\Gamma$ as $\HH^2$ quotient by $H$ and an involution
\[
\widehat{F} = (\begin{pmatrix}
        0 & \frac{1}{\sqrt{7}} \\
        -\sqrt{7} &
        0
    \end{pmatrix},\begin{pmatrix}
        0 & \sqrt{7} \\
        -\frac{1}{\sqrt{7}} &
